{
  "name": "Track job application emails from Gmail in Google Sheets with AI status detection",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Track job application emails from Gmail in Google Sheets with AI status detection\n\nStop losing track of where you applied. This workflow watches your Gmail for application confirmations, rejections, interview invites and offers, uses Google Gemini to work out the company, role and status, and keeps one row per application up to date in Google Sheets.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Check Gmail for application emails** polls every hour with a search that skips promotions and social mail.\n2. **Prepare email for AI** trims each email to the parts that matter.\n3. **Detect company, role and status** returns structured JSON (applied, assessment, interview, offer, rejected, recruiter outreach).\n4. Emails that are not about your own applications are dropped.\n5. **Update application in Google Sheets** upserts by company + role, so a rejection or interview invite updates the existing row instead of adding a new one.\n6. **Every Monday at 8am** a follow-up summary e-mail lists deadlines in the next 7 days, applications with no news for 7+ days (with thread links to chase them), this week's replies and your response rate.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add a **Gmail OAuth2** credential and a free **Google Gemini (PaLM) API** credential.\n2. Create a Google Sheet with an `Applications` tab and this header row: `application_key, company, role, status, next_step, deadline, last_update, last_subject, from, gmail_link`.\n3. Put the Sheet ID in **Config** and **Set summary settings** and connect **Google Sheets**.\n4. Put your e-mail address and follow-up delay in **Set summary settings**.\n5. Activate. The first poll reads only new emails from now on.\n\n### Customization\n- Tighten or widen the Gmail search in the trigger's *Search* filter.\n- Change `follow_up_after_days` or which statuses count as \"waiting\" in **Build follow-up summary**.\n- Add statuses (e.g. `withdrawn`) to the prompt.",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 600
      },
      "id": "713777f6-0e2b-51ab-baa4-7dcc18ea02b1",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyHour"
            }
          ]
        },
        "simple": false,
        "filters": {
          "q": "-category:promotions -category:social (application OR applying OR applied OR interview OR candidacy OR position OR role OR offer OR assessment)",
          "readStatus": "both"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "d4eb8cfa-caf9-5461-b35f-085487275338",
      "name": "Check Gmail for application emails",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmailTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
